{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1478463-online-game-players-rotation","id":1478463,"title":"Online game players rotation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-09T20:01:31-07:00","id":1478463,"title":"Online game players rotation","content":"In my now 1,5 year 'Scion 2E on Discord' game, I make 3rd recruitment phase for players. Like in clock, 9 months pass by - and even more stable players are going off the game. Why is it?<br /> <br /> In my Real Life tables rotation was a thing ( till 2020 ) - but more like after 2-3 years in it. / If player would not fallout in 1-3 starting months. / I've seen this few times. I also hear that this rotation in online games is more and more prevailing in RPG groups.<br /> <br /> <b>WHY is it, you think?</b> Why, even stables players, fallout after about 9 months of game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-15-2022, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T21:14:36-07:00","id":1478465,"title":"","content":"IME:<br /> <br /> A lot of online games, even if &quot;play&quot; only happens once a week (or whatever the schedule), tend to have a lot of &quot;off-topic&quot; social time between sessions due to the nature of having a Discord server to be chatting with your players with always there.<br /> <br /> Basically, depending on how you manage your Discord community, you run the risk of accidentally making players feel like they're gaming all the time rather than once and awhile (and they might not even recognize it). This means that burn out tends to happen faster because the game is occupying more mental space per week.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T12:00:00-07:00","id":1478504,"title":"","content":"Today I officially ended my second <b>Monarchies of Mau</b> campaign. One of leaving players said to me, bluntly - <i>'I need to rest from online play for few months - but I would gladly play more at your table if you will look for players, <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> especially'</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So Online play, probably, IS more tiresome for players than Real Life table play... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T12:30:41-07:00","id":1478507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1478463-online-game-players-rotation?p=1478504#post1478504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Online play, probably, IS more tiresome for players than Real Life table play... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>That assessment seems to check out. I remember in the middle days of MMOs (WoW and FF11) trying to get together with friends to play and after about a month or so found it impossible to sync up schedule with them. Then they all scattered off the platforms after about a season and became non-reliable as opposed to unreliable. I started thinking there's an element about online play which just makes it less &quot;serious&quot; than IRL tabletop play, easier to ignore, brush off, or grow bored with.<br /> <br /> Of course, after the advent of pandemic people find more excuses not to meet up anyway (even when fully vaccinated) so now they're all shooting themselves in the foot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T13:43:37-07:00","id":1478514,"title":"","content":"Online play doesn't have to be more tiresome for players than in-person play, it just has a different set of tools to avoid burning out because it's a different beast to disengage from and clear out of your head.<br /> <br /> I say this as someone that's been involved with 24/7 online RP chats for over twenty years. I have played a character virtually every day, for five straight years. It is a huge mental investment, probably had all sorts of negative impacts on other parts of my life for how much of my brain it occupied, and all of that. But there's a really important trick to that: you can't think about it once you're done playing for the day. When you spend two hours playing, and then five hours worrying about your character every day? It wrecks you. If you spend two hours playing instead of watching TV or playing some video games, and then when you log off, you shut that down and don't think about it again until tomorrow? You can keep going a lot longer (eventually other factors set in).<br /> <br /> This is the same problem a lot of people have with Facebook and Twitter. Spending 30 min on Twitter every day isn't going to really impact your life that much. If you can't go 15 minutes without checking your feed, it's bad for your mental health.<br /> <br /> This is why I mentioned how your run your Discord server for online games: esp. online games that are meant to replace in-person schedule TTRPG experiences. Discord, like most social media, is designed to try to get people to be on it; constantly. FOMO (fear of missing out) is a huge issue on a lot of Discord servers because you can sign off for the night and wake up to hundreds of missed messages even if you're only on a half dozen servers. FOMO is one of the biggest drives of burnout in online communities. It's why a lot of us hate that the Exalted forums are broken beyond repair and so much Exalted chat has moved to the Onyx Path and official Exalted Discord servers: it's painfully easy to just completely miss discussions you might have wanted to read, and easily miss out on participating because things have moved on already (Discord finally adding thread functions helps a little, but only a little and the best forms of that are paywalled for a reason).<br /> <br /> If you want to use Discord as an effective replacement for a weekly TTRPG session: you need to make sure that your players basically only use it once a week (for your game anyway). This doesn't mean lock it 6 days a week or something. But avoid things that encourage your server to also be an online hangout place, because your &quot;funny image&quot; channel is just going to turn into your private shared Twitter feed that lets FOMO seep into your experience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T20:44:03-07:00","id":1478546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1478463-online-game-players-rotation?p=1478514#post1478514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to use Discord as an effective replacement for a weekly TTRPG session: you need to make sure that your players basically only use it once a week (for your game anyway). This doesn't mean lock it 6 days a week or something. But avoid things that encourage your server to also be an online hangout place, because your &quot;funny image&quot; channel is just going to turn into your private shared Twitter feed that lets FOMO seep into your experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I run with Discord base and Roll20 support for battles or advanced dicerolling. However, day-to-day chat we place on Facebook Messenger, from two reasons:<br /> 1. <b>Almost all my online players</b> are from FB groups announcements. ( Beyond 3 from our old RPG club in my home city, on about 15 people I run for regularly. ) So all have FB accounts and are regulars on FB.<br /> 2. <b>FB Messenger + Discord</b> are two different channels. When FB had been halted for half a day - it was a bit grim. ANYTIME there can be service breakdown so you need to have at least two services, just in case of emergence.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental health</b> seems as good point number 3, then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-10-2022, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}